{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgArXwgXXtmRsMTzD7kru","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1809,"cache_read_input_tokens":20486,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1809},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3ff2daa-e8f8-483c-b75c-b61b05bfd2a1","uuid":"1d4f193a-b9da-43aa-aedd-8a9f9508a2c2","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:04:53.280Z","request_id":"req_011CgArXwQ9mn4dSzYxbPSND","thinking_duration_ms":4448,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgArXwgXXtmRsMTzD7kru","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K3cewjyYboah6NHLp7wAfg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-wmEw1n && python3 - <<'E'\np='scripts/deploy.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='aws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\\n'\nnew='''# Cache policy and Content-Type are always set together, per extension.\n# Never re-apply headers with `--metadata-directive REPLACE` without a\n# --content-type: it wipes the type and the site is served as octet-stream.\nSHORT=\"public, max-age=300\"          # HTML, CSS, JS: changes show up within 5 min\nLONG=\"public, max-age=2592000\"       # assets/ (30 days); rename a file to change it early\n\n# Fail if src/ holds a file type we have no Content-Type for.\nunknown=$(find src -type f ! -name '*.html' ! -name '*.js' ! -name '*.css' \\\\\n  ! -name '*.png' ! -name '*.svg' || true)\nif [ -n \"$unknown\" ]; then\n  echo \"No Content-Type mapping for:\" >&2; echo \"$unknown\" >&2; exit 1\nfi\n\n# assets/: long cache.\nfor pair in \"png:image/png\" \"svg:image/svg+xml\"; do\n  aws s3 sync src/assets/ \"s3://$BUCKET/assets/\" --delete --exclude \"*\" \\\\\n    --include \"*.${pair%%:*}\" --content-type \"${pair#*:}\" \\\\\n    --cache-control \"$LONG\" --profile \"$PROFILE\"\ndone\n\n# Everything else: short cache.\nfor pair in \"html:text/html\" \"js:application/javascript\" \"css:text/css\"; do\n  aws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --exclude \"assets/*\" --exclude \"*\" \\\\\n    --include \"*.${pair%%:*}\" --content-type \"${pair#*:}\" \\\\\n    --cache-control \"$SHORT\" --profile \"$PROFILE\"\ndone\n'''\nassert old in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nE\nbash -n scripts/deploy.sh && echo ok\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Cache-Control on deploy\n\nChanged `scripts/deploy.sh` (not run; nothing was deployed).\n\n- The single `aws s3 sync` is replaced by per-extension syncs that set `--cache-control` and an explicit `--content-type` together.\n- HTML, JS, CSS: `public, max-age=300` (5 minutes), so a new `booking.js` reaches browsers quickly.\n- `assets/` (png, svg): `public, max-age=2592000` (30 days).\n- Content types are explicit (`text/html`, `application/javascript`, `text/css`, `image/png`, `image/svg+xml`). This avoids the `binary/octet-stream` trap described in `notes/a-cache-header-tweak-served-my-whole-site-as-octet-stream.md`. I did not use `--metadata-directive REPLACE`.\n- The script fails early if `src/` contains a file type with no mapping.\n- `--delete` still works, applied per pass within each file type.\n- The CloudFront invalidation is unchanged.\n\nNotes:\n- Assets aren't fingerprinted, so a replaced `logo.png` can stay cached up to 30 days. Rename the file or shorten `LONG` if that matters.\n- Visitors who already cached the old `booking.js` with no header keep it until their browser revalidates. The new headers only apply after the next deploy.\n- After deploying, check with `curl -sI <site>/booking.js`. It should show `content-type: application/javascript` and the `cache-control` header.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1809,"cache_read_input_tokens":20486,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1809},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3ff2daa-e8f8-483c-b75c-b61b05bfd2a1","uuid":"dc1c7866-0062-4b4e-a35b-13289caa9cd8","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:05:00.214Z","request_id":"req_011CgArXwQ9mn4dSzYxbPSND","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01K3cewjyYboah6NHLp7wAfg":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-wmEw1n && python3 - <<'E'\np='scripts/deploy.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='aws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\\n'\nnew='''# Cache policy and Content-Type are always set together, per extension.\n# Never re-apply headers with `--metadata-directive REPLACE` without a\n# --content-type: it wipes the type and the site is served as octet-stream.\nSHORT=\"public, max-age=300\"          # HTML, CSS, JS: changes show up within 5 min\nLONG=\"public, max-age=2592000\"       # assets/ (30 days); rename a file to change it early\n\n# Fail if src/ holds a file type we have no Content-Type for.\nunknown=$(find src -type f ! -name '*.html' ! -name '*.js' ! -name '*.css' \\\\\n  ! -name '*.png' ! -name '*.svg' || true)\nif [ -n \"$unknown\" ]; then\n  echo \"No Content-Type mapping for:\" >&2; echo \"$unknown\" >&2; exit 1\nfi\n\n# assets/: long cache.\nfor pair in \"png:image/png\" \"svg:image/svg+xml\"; do\n  aws s3 sync src/assets/ \"s3://$BUCKET/assets/\" --delete --exclude \"*\" \\\\\n    --include \"*.${pair%%:*}\" --content-type \"${pair#*:}\" \\\\\n    --cache-control \"$LONG\" --profile \"$PROFILE\"\ndone\n\n# Everything else: short cache.\nfor pair in \"html:text/html\" \"js:application/javascript\" \"css:text/css\"; do\n  aws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --exclude \"assets/*\" --exclude \"*\" \\\\\n    --include \"*.${pair%%:*}\" --content-type \"${pair#*:}\" \\\\\n    --cache-control \"$SHORT\" --profile \"$PROFILE\"\ndone\n'''\nassert old in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nE\nbash -n scripts/deploy.sh && echo ok\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Cache-Control on deploy\n\nChanged `scripts/deploy.sh` (not run; nothing was deployed).\n\n- The single `aws s3 sync` is replaced by per-extension syncs that set `--cache-control` and an explicit `--content-type` together.\n- HTML, JS, CSS: `public, max-age=300` (5 minutes), so a new `booking.js` reaches browsers quickly.\n- `assets/` (png, svg): `public, max-age=2592000` (30 days).\n- Content types are explicit (`text/html`, `application/javascript`, `text/css`, `image/png`, `image/svg+xml`). This avoids the `binary/octet-stream` trap described in `notes/a-cache-header-tweak-served-my-whole-site-as-octet-stream.md`. I did not use `--metadata-directive REPLACE`.\n- The script fails early if `src/` contains a file type with no mapping.\n- `--delete` still works, applied per pass within each file type.\n- The CloudFront invalidation is unchanged.\n\nNotes:\n- Assets aren't fingerprinted, so a replaced `logo.png` can stay cached up to 30 days. Rename the file or shorten `LONG` if that matters.\n- Visitors who already cached the old `booking.js` with no header keep it until their browser revalidates. The new headers only apply after the next deploy.\n- After deploying, check with `curl -sI <site>/booking.js`. It should show `content-type: application/javascript` and the `cache-control` header.\nE"}}}
